  "rating": {
    "inherent": "critical",
    "residual": "high",
    "forecast": "critical",
    "rationale": "Present risk is driven by untrusted supplier invoices reaching S3 payment scheduling and S2 bank-detail changes. The only declared preventive gate on sensitive actions is a structural human approval control with approval_review_mode set to model_summary, so rubric step 2 lowers risk but cannot reduce summary-gated payment below high when inherent is critical, and bank-update residual floors at moderate. Broad ERP credentials preserve a separate high residual confused-deputy path. Forecast rises to critical because ctl.clerk_approval is partially dependent and is specifically weakened by model_upgrade and approval fatigue in a design that upgrades the model without separate review and processes roughly 150 approvals per clerk per day. Manual validation was applied against the provided schema and validation checklist; this assessment reflects declared design and configuration, not observed runtime behavior."
  },
